// ============================================================================
// Detection: Unexpected East-West (Pod-to-Pod) Network Flow
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1046 - Network Service Discovery
// Source: Container Network Logs (ACNS / Hubble)  [TEMPLATE — see notes below]
// ============================================================================
//
// STATUS: TEMPLATE / UNVERIFIED. This is the network-plane complement to
// lateral-movement.kql (which is audit/token-based). It requires the pod-to-pod
// flow-log plane, which is NOT enabled by default.
//
// ENABLEMENT (two steps):
//   1. ACNS observability — set in infrastructure/modules/aks_cluster.bicep
//      (networkProfile.advancedNetworking.observability). This turns on Hubble.
//   2. Stored "Container Network Logs" → Log Analytics — a SEPARATE, newer AKS
//      feature (flow logs land in a resource-specific table, queryable with KQL).
//      Its enablement path and exact TABLE NAME + SCHEMA are evolving — CONFIRM
//      against current AKS docs and a captured sample before trusting this query.
//      The table below is a placeholder; adjust field names to the real schema.
//
// Once real flow-log data exists, capture a sample and tune this exactly the way
// the audit detections were tuned — the field paths here are best-effort, not verified.
//
// Idea: an attacker moving laterally opens NEW cross-namespace pod-to-pod flows —
// connections between namespaces that normally never talk. Baseline the legitimate
// pairs first, then alert on the rest.

// HOW THIS DETECTION WORKS (once the flow-log plane exists)
// ---------------------------------------------------------
// Unlike the other detections, this reads the NETWORK plane (pod-to-pod flow logs
// from Cilium/Hubble), not the API audit log. The idea: an attacker mapping the
// cluster or pivoting between workloads opens NEW east-west connections between
// namespaces that normally never talk (T1046 Network Service Discovery). We keep
// only cross-namespace, successfully-forwarded flows and roll them up per pod-pair.
//
// TABLE: RetinaNetworkFlowLogs — PLACEHOLDER name; confirm against the real
//        Container Network Logs schema before trusting this.

// CONFIRM the table name once Container Network Logs are enabled (placeholder):
RetinaNetworkFlowLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)        // recent window first
| where FlowType == "L3_L4"            // adjust to real schema — keep network-layer connection flows
| where Verdict == "FORWARDED"         // only flows the network policy ALLOWED (a real connection happened)
| where SourceNamespace != DestinationNamespace          // cross-namespace = east-west
| where SourceNamespace !in ("kube-system", "gatekeeper-system")   // baseline / allowlist
// summarize = aggregate. Per (source pod, dest pod, 5-min bucket) count the flows
// and collect the DISTINCT destination ports touched (make_set) — a pod hitting
// many ports on a peer looks like scanning/discovery.
| summarize Flows = count(), Ports = make_set(DestinationPort)
        by SourceNamespace, SourcePod = SourcePodName,
           DestinationNamespace, DestinationPod = DestinationPodName, bin(TimeGenerated, 5m)  // bin() = fixed 5-min time buckets
| extend MitreTechnique = "T1046"    // tag with the ATT&CK technique
